    typicalWorkday: ["Morning: prepare a quarterly portfolio review for a retired couple, checking allocations against their plan. Midday: sit in on the senior advisor's client meetings, taking notes on action items. Afternoon: research a client's question about 529 plans, update financial planning software with a new client's data, and study an hour for the Series 66."],
    aiImpact: ["AI handles more of the portfolio mechanics and report generation, which raises rather than lowers the value of the human relationship layer: trust does not automate. A massive generational wealth transfer plus retiring advisors means strong long-term demand for new advisors."],
    requiredSkills: ["Communication and trust-building","portfolio and retirement planning basics","Excel","discretion","patience","licensing exams (Series 7/66, supported by the firm)","long-term relationship instincts"],
